"""Verifier for one task bundle. tests/test.sh runs it as /tests/validate.py.

Reads the two deliverables from /output, grades them against the pristine tree
in /grade/<repo>, and writes, under /logs/verifier:

    stages.json    the observations the compiled relations in test_output.py read
    reward.json    deterministic_channel, judged_channel, reward (the one reward carrier)
    reasons.json   per-test outcome, dropped diff sections, and why a score is zero
    if_score.json  instruction-following constraints, reported apart from the reward

Every stage starts from the pristine commit (git checkout and clean), so no
stage sees another stage's edits. A test that cannot be decided fails; nothing
passes on missing evidence. An infrastructure failure still writes defined
zeros, with reasons.json marking the trial invalid.

Also `validate.py measure ROUNDS` prints the fail-to-pass and pass-to-pass sets
measured in this image: the bundle builder calls it once before freezing.
"""

